---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import {url} from '../lib/base';
import {records} from '../lib/catalogue';
const rows = [["cpo-2030","Optical interconnects","CPO Update: The Company-by-Company Map to 2030","cpo-update-the-company-by-company","preview","Switch optics are moving into deployment before accelerator-side optics. The source models a roughly $100bn market by 2030; this is a scenario, not an established market size.","NVIDIA; Broadcom; Coherent; Lumentum; Lambda","CPO, NPO, OBO, pluggables, OCS","Track switch shipments, optical engine yields and scale-up qualification."],["asic-era","Accelerators","The ASIC Era Is Coming: NVIDIA and Its Rivals After Jensen","the-asic-era-is-coming-nvidia-and","preview","Custom accelerators can reduce recurring inference costs at sufficient scale, while external design partners retain valuable implementation expertise. Leadership-related premises require fresh verification.","NVIDIA; Google; Broadcom; MediaTek; Marvell; AMD","ASIC, TPU, SerDes, HBM","Track workload migration, design wins and total cost per inference."],["dram-economics","Memory","When Will Next Generation DRAM Make Economic Sense?","when-will-next-generation-dram-make","expert preview","The interview emphasizes good dies per unit cost rather than architectural labels. Vertical cells and stacked DRAM require economical fabrication and throughput.","Memory makers; equipment suppliers","4F², 3D DRAM, EUV, HBM","Track yield, process steps, equipment productivity and qualification."],["substrates","Packaging","Why Exactly Are Substrates the Bottleneck?","why-exactly-are-substrates-the-bottleneck","preview","Larger AI packages increase demand for fine wiring and ABF substrates; usable output can lag nominal capacity. The stated 2031 shortage horizon is a source forecast.","TSMC; Intel; Ajinomoto","ABF, T-glass, CCL, CoWoS, EMIB","Track substrate dimensions, layer count, material supply and good-unit capacity."],["optics-deal","Optical interconnects","Marvell Buys Lumentum: What If NVIDIA Set Up the Play?","marvell-buys-lumentum-what-if-nvidia","speculative preview","The author proposes four hypothetical strategic explanations involving optics, TPU suppliers, NVLink and NVHBM. Neither the transaction premise nor NVIDIA involvement is independently verified here.","Marvell; Lumentum; NVIDIA; Google; Broadcom","Lasers, NVLink, NVHBM","Verify transaction disclosures and actual customer design wins before accepting any scenario."],["amd-competition","Accelerators","Can AMD Beat NVIDIA? Part 2","can-amd-beat-nvidia-part2-vera-rubins","preview","The source discusses Meta recommendation-model training comparisons and AI-assisted kernel porting. Results depend on workload, GPU count and power caps; they cannot establish universal performance parity.","AMD; NVIDIA; Meta","MI350X, B200, HBM4, CUDA, kernels","Track independently reproducible benchmarks, software migration cost and rack deployments."],["physical-ai","Physical AI","Physical AI Explained","physical-ai-explained","archive extract","Sensor inputs, learned decisions and control loops enable adaptive machines. Commercial maturity varies sharply across factories, logistics, vehicles and humanoids.","NVIDIA; Mobileye; Waymo; Amazon; Symbotic; Unitree; Cognex","Sensors, edge compute, robotics, control","Track paid deployments, uptime, safety and economics per task."],["euv-economics","Manufacturing","EUV Technology and Economics","expert-call-euv-technology-and-economics","expert preview","Lithography economics depend on throughput, yield and avoided process steps, not just machine price. High NA improves resolution but introduces process-control challenges.","ASML; chipmakers","DUV, EUV, High NA","Track cost per good wafer, utilization and customer qualification."],["ai-advertising","AI monetisation","How AI Is Changing Advertising Market","how-ai-is-changing-meta-advertising","expert preview","The interview separates predictive model development from product integration for advertiser objectives. Incremental performance, rather than attributed conversions alone, is a key commercial question.","Meta","Advertising AI, optimization, agents, smart glasses","Track incrementality, advertiser spend and privacy constraints."],["cerebras-yield","Manufacturing","Cerebras's Mass Production Challenges","cerebrass-mass-production-challenges","archive extract","Wafer-scale redundancy can bypass defective cores, but simplified core-count models are not actual manufacturing yields. Routing and shared circuitry matter.","Cerebras; NVIDIA; TSMC","WSE-3, redundancy, NoC, yield","Track qualified wafer output, testing and repair limits."],["micron-fabs","Memory","Another Side of Micron, Seen from Its Taiwan Fabs","expert-call-report-another-side-of","expert preview","The source explores HBM manufacturing, yield improvement and workforce concerns through an expert account; testimony should not be treated as company-wide verified fact.","Micron","HBM, yield, fab operations","Track manufacturing execution, staffing and disclosed output."],["optical-testing","Optical interconnects","Co-Packaged, Near-Packaged, Always Tested","co-packaged-near-packaged-always","preview","Optical testing demand may expand regardless of whether near-package or co-packaged optics is adopted first. The timing and supplier revenue implications remain conditional.","Optical test suppliers","CPO, NPO, optical testing","Track test intensity, equipment orders and production qualification."]];
const [technologies,companies,sectors]=await Promise.all([records('technologies'),records('companies'),records('sectors')]);
const paywalled=rows.filter(r=>String(r[4]).includes('preview')).length;
const groups=[...new Set(rows.map(r=>r[1]))];
const matches=(items,terms)=>items.filter(x=>terms.split(/[,;]/).some(t=>{const q=t.trim().toLowerCase();return q.length>2 && (x.title||'').toLowerCase().includes(q)})).slice(0,8);
---
<Site title="AI & semiconductor intelligence" active="Intelligence" description="Source-linked research on AI infrastructure, semiconductor supply chains and commercial catalysts.">
<div class="container page intelligence">
<div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Research dossier / November 2026 archive</span><h1>AI & semiconductor intelligence</h1><p>From fabrication constraints to AI monetisation: {rows.length} source-linked research briefs.</p></div>
<div class="data-note">Independent editorial summaries of Damnang Research archive extracts supplied by the reader. {paywalled} of {rows.length} posts are marked paywalled in the archive. No subscription-only text is reproduced. Claims and forecasts have not been independently verified. <a href="https://www.damnang.com/archive?sort=new">Original archive ↗</a></div>
<nav class="topics" aria-label="Research themes">{groups.map(g=><a href={'#'+g.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}>{g}</a>)}</nav>
<section class="chain"><h2>Value chain</h2><p>Manufacturing → Packaging → Memory → Accelerators → Optical interconnects → Physical AI & AI monetisation</p><p>Research lens: production constraints, cost per useful output, supplier bargaining power and adoption milestones.</p></section>
{groups.map(g=><section class="group" id={g.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}><h2>{g}</h2><div class="briefs">{rows.filter(r=>r[1]===g).map(r=><article id={r[0]}><span class="eyebrow">{r[4]} · Damnang Research</span><h3><a href={'https://www.damnang.com/p/'+r[3]}>{r[2]} ↗</a></h3><p>{r[5]}</p><p><strong>Technology:</strong> {r[7]}</p><p><strong>Company exposure:</strong> {r[6]}</p><p><strong>What to monitor:</strong> {r[8]}</p>{matches(technologies,r[7]).length>0&&<div class="related"><strong>Related atlas technologies</strong>{matches(technologies,r[7]).map(t=><a href={url('/tech/'+t.id+'/')}>{t.title}</a>)}</div>}{matches(companies,r[6]).length>0&&<div class="related"><strong>Related company profiles</strong>{matches(companies,r[6]).map(c=><a href={url('/companies/'+c.id+'/')}>{c.title}</a>)}</div>}</article>)}</div></section>)}
<p><a href={url('/research/')}>Evidence methodology</a> · <a href={url('/roadmaps/')}>Technology roadmaps</a> · <a href={url('/sectors/')}>All sectors</a></p></div></Site>
<style>
.intelligence{padding-bottom:3rem}.topics,.related{display:flex;gap:.55rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.topics a,.related a{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;padding:.35rem .55rem;font-size:.85rem}.chain,.briefs article{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);border-radius:8px;padding:1.2rem;margin:1rem 0}.group{scroll-margin-top:5rem;margin-top:2rem}.briefs h3{margin:.5rem 0}.briefs p{line-height:1.6;margin:.65rem 0}.related{margin-top:1rem;align-items:center}.related strong{width:100%;font-size:.8rem}.chain p{line-height:1.6}
</style>